ompt plus the proposed tokens in one forward pass, computing logits for every position in that sequence. This lets it verify multiple draft tokens at once instead of generating them one by one.\n\nThe key trick is rejection sampling. For each proposed token, the target model compares its own probability for that token with the draft model\u2019s probability. If the target model\u2019s probability is at least as high, the token is accepted. If it is lower, the token is rejected and a new token is sampled from a corrected distribution that favors the target model\u2019s probabilities while preserving the target model\u2019s exact output distribution. After the first rejected token, the remaining draft tokens are discarded. Because every accepted or resampled token is drawn from the target model\u2019s conditional distribution, the final sequence has the same distribution as ordinary autoregressive decoding with the target model alone.\n\nIn practice, speedup depends on how often the draft model is correct, the cost of running the target model on the longer speculative sequence, and the overhead of running the draft model. A good draft model that matches the target model\u2019s style and task can accept many tokens, reducing the number of expensive target-model steps. The speedup is limited when the draft model is too small or poorly aligned, causing many rejections, and when the target model\u2019s verification pass is not much cheaper per token than generating one token, especially for short sequences or high-batch workloads.\"\n\nCount", "top2": [[[1596, -0.002059970749542117], [22916, -6.88720703125]], [[1144, -1.7166285033454187e-05], [4087, -11.819669723510742]], [[4087, -0.213497593998909], [310, -1.6600346565246582]], [[1156, -0.0020912683103233576], [303, -6.246794700622559]], [[579, -0.2518881857395172], [25, -1.7952040433883667]], [[1622, -0.010124022141098976], [3296, -4.839090347290039]], [[25, -0.33031508326530457], [13, -1.2881110906600952]], [[59987, -0